ted  well i think that uh the stars aligned  in the worst possible way in the last  election  we all witnessed it i mean i grew up in  l.a george gascon claims to be  progressive this is not  progressive this is regressive this  these policies take us right back to the  revolving door  that we had going in the 70s and 80s  that that resulted in the murders of  people like paulie klaus and marcy  nicholas  this is the kind of stuff that enacted  reforms like three strikes like the gun  enhancements  and and like victim rights in california  this is outrageous and i just heard that  for the first time just now that they're  saying a majority of the victims don't  support that  i was a prosecutor for 26 years i  attended parole hearings  for 17 of those as i worked in the  orange county homicide unit  that is there's no way that that is a  true statistic unless they did their own  poll of like  four people that are their ideological  ilk that is an outrageous thing to say  it is absolutely untrue victims who lose  loved ones due to violent crime  want justice for the people that were  taken away from them  and under current california law there  are ways to do that and george gascon  has  unilaterally decided he's not going to  impose gun enhancements gang  enhancements  strikes and the effect on my clients i  represent five of these families  one of whom is tonya owen who i just  heard on on the clip  her husband was a a sheriff's sergeant  who responded to a burglary  the person he encountered was a violent  felon with an extensive criminal history  a documented gang member who ambushed  him shot him once  disabled him walked over to him  and executed him shot him three times in  the face  and then another time in the badge  sending a message  right that guy because of george  gascon's policies  could be released as soon as eight years  from today  so if it takes us another year or two to  get to trial that's  literally less than six years in  california state prison